{"text": "Hargrove Ellison & Pruitt LLP\n418 Commerce Street, 9th Floor\n\nNashville, TN 37219\n\nTel. 615.555.0127 | Fax 615.555.0128\n\nMay 6, 2026\n\nVIA CERTIFIED MAIL AND EMAIL (kbasaran@cumberlandyards.example)\n\nMr. Kerem Basaran, Managing Member\n\nCumberland Yards Property Group, L.L.C.\n\nPO Box 40117\n\nFranklin, TN 37065\n\nRe: Demand for return of security deposit and rent abatement — Suite 210,\n1700 Riverfront Parkway (the \"Premises\"); Our File No. 26-0393-L\n\nDear Mr. Basaran:\n\nThis firm represents Wren & Thistle Bakehouse, LLC (\"Wren & Thistle\") and its\nowner, Ms. Saoirse Ní Dhomhnaill-Parker, in connection with the Commercial\nLease dated August 1, 2022 (the \"Lease\") between Wren & Thistle and Cumberland\nYards Property Group, L.L.C. (\"Cumberland Yards\"). Please direct all further\ncommunication about this matter to me and not to our client.\n\nAs you know, on January 19, 2026 a sprinkler main failed in the ceiling above the\nPremises and flooded the kitchen and retail floor. Your own contractor, Dixon\nRestoration Services, confirmed in its report of January 27, 2026 that the failure\nwas caused by a corroded fitting in the building's common fire-suppression\nsystem, which is the Landlord's responsibility under Section 9.1 of the Lease. The\nPremises were unusable from January 19 until April 17, 2026, a period of nearly\nthree months. Throughout that period Cumberland Yards continued to draw base\nrent of $6,240 per month from our client's account by ACH.\n\nSection 14.2 of the Lease provides that rent abates in full for any period in which\nthe Premises are untenantable through no fault of the Tenant. Our client vacated\n\non April 30, 2026 after giving proper notice and returned the keys to your\nproperty manager, Marguerite Odom, who signed the walk-through checklist\nwithout exception. Ms. Odom then told Ms. Ní Dhomhnaill-Parker by text message\nthat the deposit was being \"held pending review.\" There is nothing to review.\n\nAccordingly, Wren & Thistle demands payment of the following:\n\n Return of the security deposit: $18,500.00\n Refund of rent collected during the abatement period (three months):\n$18,720.00\n Spoiled inventory and lost equipment, per the schedule already sent to you:\napproximately $11,000\n Total: $48,220.00\n\nPayment must be received no later than May 20, 2026. Funds may be wired to our\nIOLTA trust account at Volunteer State Bank & Trust, routing no. 087321579,\naccount no. 0044-718-3392, referencing our file number above.\n\nIf payment is not received by that date, we are instructed to file suit in the\nChancery Court for Davidson County without further notice, and to seek the bad-\nfaith damages and attorney's fees available under Tenn. Code Ann. § 66-28-301\nand the Lease. This letter is sent for settlement purposes under Rule 408 and is\nwithout prejudice to any of our client's rights, all of which are reserved.\n\nVery truly yours,\n\nTheodore R. Pruitt IV\n\nTN BPR No. 029914\n\nDirect: (615) 555-0131 | trpruitt@hep-law.example\n\ncc: S. Ní Dhomhnaill-Parker (by email)", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 476 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Kerem Basaran", "Saoirse Ní Dhomhnaill-Parker", "Marguerite Odom", "Theodore R. Pruitt IV", "S. Ní Dhomhnaill-Parker"], "companies": ["Hargrove Ellison & Pruitt LLP", "Cumberland Yards Property Group, L.L.C.", "Wren & Thistle Bakehouse, LLC", "Dixon Restoration Services", "Cumberland Yards", "Volunteer State Bank & Trust", "hep-law"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 152.90000000037253, "modelMs": 24554.300000000745, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "Hargrove Ellison & Pruitt LLP", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Hargrove Ell